msgstr "If disabled, they need to ask admins to do it for them."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_portal_allow_edit_email_forward"
msgstr "Allow users to add, remove, edit mail forward"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_portal_allow_edit_email_forward_help"
msgstr "If disabled, they need to ask admins to do it for them."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_root_access_name"
msgstr "Change root password"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_root_access_explain"
msgstr ""
"On Linux systems, 'root' is the absolute admin. In YunoHost context, "
"direct 'root' SSH login is by default disable - except from the local "
"network of the server. Members of the 'admins' group can use the sudo "
"command to act as root from the command line. However, it can be helpful "
"to have a (robust) root password to debug the system if for some reason "
"regular admins can not login anymore."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_root_password"
msgstr "New root password"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_root_password_confirm"
msgstr "New root password (confirm)"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_experimental_name"
msgstr "Experimental"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_security_experimental_enabled"
msgstr "Experimental security features"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_security_experimental_enabled_help"
msgstr ""
"Enable experimental security features (don't enable this if you don't "
"know what you're doing!)"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_email_name"
msgstr "Email"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_pop3_name"
msgstr "POP3"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_pop3_enabled"
msgstr "Enable POP3"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_pop3_enabled_help"
msgstr ""
"Enable the POP3 protocol for the mail server. POP3 is an older protocol "
"to access mailboxes from email clients and is more lightweight, but has "
"less features than IMAP (enabled by default)"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_name"
msgstr "SMTP"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_allow_ipv6"
msgstr "Allow IPv6"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_allow_ipv6_help"
msgstr "Allow the use of IPv6 to receive and send mail"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_enabled"
msgstr "Enable SMTP relay"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_enabled_help"
msgstr ""
"Enable the SMTP relay to use in order to send mail instead of this "
"yunohost instance. Useful if you are in one of this situation: your 25 "
"port is blocked by your ISP or VPS provider, you have a residential IP "
"listed on DUHL, you are not able to configure reverse DNS or this server "
"is not directly exposed on the internet and you want use an other one to "
"send mails."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_host"
msgstr "SMTP relay host"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_port"
msgstr "SMTP relay port"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_user"
msgstr "SMTP relay user"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_relay_password"
msgstr "SMTP relay password"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_backup_mx_domains"
msgstr "Domains to act as secondary MX for"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_backup_mx_domains_help"
msgstr ""
"Allow this server to act as a backup *secondary* MX domain for the listed"
" domain. This means that if the main MX for the domain is not reachable "
"(for example because of an outage), mails will still be sent to this "
"server, which will keep them during a maximum of 20 days and try to relay"
" them to the real destination once it goes back up. Several domains can "
"be provided, separated by commas."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_backup_mx_emails_whitelisted"
msgstr "SMTP backup MX emails whitelist"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_smtp_backup_mx_emails_whitelisted_help"
msgstr ""
"When acting as a secondary MX, the exhaustive list of allowed recipient's"
" email addresses must be provided (otherwise mails will be refused and "
"discarded). Several entries can be provided, separated by commas."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_antispam_name"
msgstr "Antispam"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_enable_blocklists"
msgstr "Enable blocklists for incoming traffic"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_enable_blocklists_help"
msgstr ""
"Blocks servers listed by spamcop.net, spamhaus.org and abuseat.org to "
"prevent spam. However, this may cause delivery problems for some harmless"
" mail servers which may be listed by those third parties, in which case "
"mail sent from these servers won't be received."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_misc_name"
msgstr "Other"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_backup_name"
msgstr "Backup"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_backup_compress_tar_archives"
msgstr "Compress backups"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_backup_compress_tar_archives_help"
msgstr ""
"When creating new backups, compress the archives (.tar.gz) instead of "
"uncompressed archives (.tar). N.B. : enabling this option means create "
"lighter backup archives, but the initial backup procedure will be "
"significantly longer and heavy on CPU."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_network_name"
msgstr "Network"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_exposure"
msgstr "IP versions to consider for DNS configuration and diagnosis"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_exposure_help"
msgstr ""
"NB: This only affects the recommended DNS configuration and diagnosis "
"checks. This does not affect system configurations."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_custom_resolvers_enabled"
msgstr "Use custom DNS resolvers"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_custom_resolvers_enabled_help"
msgstr ""
"By default, YunoHost uses a list of trustworthy resolvers located in "
"Europe. Advanced users may want to specify custom resolvers instead."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_custom_resolvers_list"
msgstr "Custom resolvers' addresses"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_dns_custom_resolvers_list_help"
msgstr ""
"A list of at least 2 DNS resolvers per IP protocol in use (IPv4/IPv6). "
"Example: 89.234.141.66 45.67.81.23 2a00:5881:8100:1000::3 2a0c:e300::1337"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_name"
msgstr "TLS-passthrough / SNI-based forwarding"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_enabled"
msgstr "Enable TLS-passthrough / SNI-based forwarding"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_enabled_help"
msgstr ""
"This is an advanced feature to reverse-proxy an entire domain to another "
"machine *without* decrypting the traffic. Useful when you want to expose "
"several machines behind the same IP but still allow each machine to "
"handle the SSL termination."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_explain"
msgstr ""
"This feature is ADVANCED and EXPERIMENTAL and will trigger major changes "
"in the nginx configuration of this server. Please DO NOT use it if you "
"don't know what you are doing! In particular, you must be aware that "
"fail2ban cannot be implemented on the proxied server (nftables cannot ban"
" malicious traffic as all IP packets appear as coming from the front "
"server). In addition, for now the proxied server's nginx configuration "
"needs to manually tweaked to accept the `proxy_protocol`."

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_list"
msgstr "List of forwarding"

#: share/config_global.toml
msgid "global_settings_setting_tls_passthrough_list_help"
msgstr ""
"Should be a list of DOMAIN;DESTINATION;PORT, such as "
"domain.tld;192.168.1.42;443 or domain.tld;server.local;8123"

#: src/__init__.py:142
msgid "yunohost_not_installed"
msgstr ""
"YunoHost is not correctly installed. Please run 'yunohost tools "
"postinstall'"

#: src/app.py:328
msgid "app_upgrade_url_required"
msgstr ""
"This app does not exists (anymore?) in the catalog, you must therefore "
"take care of upgrades manually. <br/><small>From the command line, you "
"can use `yunohost app upgrade <app>` and provide the url of the repo "
"using the `-u` option.</small>"

#: src/app.py:355
msgid "app_upgrade_specific_channel_msg"
msgstr ""
"Note that you're currently using `{channel}` as source for upgrades. Be "
"sure to check the ongoing discussion [here]({pr_url})."

#: src/app.py:382
msgid "app_upgrade_bad_quality"
msgstr ""
