"This domain's nginx configuration appears to have been modified manually,"
" and prevents YunoHost from diagnosing if it's reachable on HTTP."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:51
msgid "diagnosis_http_nginx_conf_not_up_to_date_details"
msgstr ""
"To fix the situation, inspect the difference from the command line using "
"<cmd>yunohost tools regen-conf nginx --dry-run --with-diff</cmd> and if "
"you're ok with it, apply the changes with <cmd>yunohost tools regen-conf "
"nginx --force</cmd>."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:57
msgid "diagnosis_http_special_use_tld"
msgstr ""
"Domain {domain} is based on a special-use top-level domain (TLD) such as "
".local or .test and is therefore not expected to be exposed outside the "
"local network."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:109
msgid "diagnosis_http_hairpinning_issue"
msgstr "Your local network does not seem to have hairpinning enabled."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:110
msgid "diagnosis_http_hairpinning_issue_details"
msgstr ""
"This is probably because of your ISP box / router. As a result, people "
"from outside your local network will be able to access your server as "
"expected, but not people from inside the local network (like you, "
"probably?) when using the domain name or global IP. You may be able to "
"improve the situation by having a look at <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/dns_local_network'>https://doc.yunohost.org/dns_local_network</a>"

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:133
msgid "diagnosis_http_could_not_diagnose"
msgstr ""
"Could not diagnose if domains are reachable from outside in "
"IPv{ipversion}."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:134
msgid "diagnosis_http_could_not_diagnose_details"
msgstr "Error: {error}"

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:159 src/diagnosers/21-web.py:215
msgid "diagnosis_http_ok"
msgstr "Domain {domain} is reachable through HTTP from outside the local network."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:169
msgid "diagnosis_http_unreachable"
msgstr ""
"Domain {domain} appears unreachable through HTTP from outside the local "
"network."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py:201 src/diagnosers/21-web.py:221
msgid "diagnosis_http_partially_unreachable"
msgstr ""
"Domain {domain} appears unreachable through HTTP from outside the local "
"network in IPv{failed}, though it works in IPv{passed}."

#: src/diagnosers/21-web.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_web"
msgstr "Web"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:89
msgid "diagnosis_mail_outgoing_port_25_blocked"
msgstr ""
"The SMTP mail server cannot send emails to other servers because outgoing"
" port 25 is blocked in IPv{ipversion}."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:91
msgid "diagnosis_mail_outgoing_port_25_blocked_details"
msgstr ""
"You should first try to unblock outgoing port 25 in your internet router "
"interface or your hosting provider interface. (Some hosting providers may"
" require you to send them a support ticket for this)."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:92
msgid "diagnosis_mail_outgoing_port_25_blocked_relay_vpn"
msgstr ""
"Some providers won't let you unblock outgoing port 25 because they don't "
"care about Net Neutrality.<br> - Some of them provide the alternative of "
"<a href='https://doc.yunohost.org/email_configure_relay'>using a mail "
"server relay</a> though it implies that the relay will be able to spy on "
"your email traffic.<br>- A privacy-friendly alternative is to use a VPN "
"*with a dedicated public IP* to bypass these kinds of limits. See <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/vpn_advantage'>https://doc.yunohost.org/vpn_advantage</a><br>-"
" You can also consider switching to <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/providers/isp'>a more net neutrality-"
"friendly provider</a>"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:116
msgid "diagnosis_mail_ehlo_could_not_diagnose"
msgstr ""
"Could not diagnose if postfix mail server is reachable from the outside "
"in IPv{ipversion}."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:117
msgid "diagnosis_mail_ehlo_could_not_diagnose_details"
msgstr "Error: {error}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:139
msgid "diagnosis_mail_ehlo_wrong"
msgstr ""
"A different SMTP mail server answers on IPv{ipversion}. Your server will "
"probably not be able to receive emails."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:140
msgid "diagnosis_mail_ehlo_wrong_details"
msgstr ""
"The EHLO received by the remote diagnoser in IPv{ipversion} is different "
"from your server's domain.<br>Received EHLO: "
"<code>{wrong_ehlo}</code><br>Expected: <code>{right_ehlo}</code><br>The "
"most common cause for this issue is that port 25 <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/admin/get_started/post_install/dns_config/'>is"
" not correctly forwarded to your server</a>. Alternatively, make sure "
"that no firewall or reverse-proxy is interfering."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:154 src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:160
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_nok_details"
msgstr ""
"You should first try to configure reverse DNS with "
"<code>{ehlo_domain}</code> in your internet router interface or your "
"hosting provider interface. (Some hosting providers may require you to "
"send them a support ticket for this)."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:155
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_nok_alternatives_6"
msgstr ""
"Some providers won't let you configure your reverse DNS (or their feature"
" might be broken…). If your reverse DNS is correctly configured for IPv4,"
" you can try disabling the use of IPv6 when sending emails by running "
"<cmd>yunohost settings set email.smtp.smtp_allow_ipv6 -v off</cmd>. Note:"
" this last solution means that you won't be able to send or receive "
"emails from the few IPv6-only servers out there."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:161
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_nok_alternatives_4"
msgstr ""
"Some providers won't let you configure your reverse DNS (or their feature"
" might be broken…). If you are experiencing issues because of this, "
"consider the following solutions:<br> - Some ISP provide the alternative "
"of <a href='https://doc.yunohost.org/email_configure_relay'>using a mail "
"server relay</a> though it implies that the relay will be able to spy on "
"your email traffic.<br>- A privacy-friendly alternative is to use a VPN "
"*with a dedicated public IP* to bypass this kind of limits. See <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/vpn_advantage'>https://doc.yunohost.org/vpn_advantage</a><br>-"
" Or it's possible to <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/providers/isp'>switch to a different "
"provider</a>"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:179
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_dns_missing"
msgstr ""
"No reverse DNS is defined in IPv{ipversion}. Some emails may fail to get "
"delivered or be flagged as spam."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:189
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_different_from_ehlo_domain_details"
msgstr ""
"Current reverse DNS: <code>{rdns_domain}</code><br>Expected value: "
"<code>{ehlo_domain}</code>"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:199
msgid "diagnosis_mail_fcrdns_different_from_ehlo_domain"
msgstr ""
"Reverse DNS is not correctly configured for IPv{ipversion}. Some emails "
"may fail to get delivered or be flagged as spam."

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:243
msgid "diagnosis_mail_blocklist_reason"
msgstr "The blocklist reason is: {reason}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:245
msgid "diagnosis_mail_blocklist_reason_openresolver"
msgstr ""
"It looks like the reason mentions 'open resolver'.<br/>This usually means"
" your server is not using its local DNS, but a public, open, one.<br/> "
"Check the contents of <code>/etc/resolv.conf</code>, it should contain "
"<code>nameserver 127.0.0.1</code>.<br/>Since this file is usually "
"automatically generated, do not edit it manually. Check your DHCP "
"settings, or your VPN settings if you are using one, or if you used a "
"Debian image made by, for example, a VPS provider, look for a "
"<code>cloudinit</code> configuration.<br/> You are most welcome on the "
"YunoHost support channels to get help on this issue.<br/> The verbatim "
"blacklist reason is: {reason}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:248
msgid "diagnosis_mail_blocklist_website"
msgstr ""
"After identifying why you are listed and fixing it, feel free to ask for "
"your IP or domain to be removed on {blocklist_website}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:262
msgid "diagnosis_mail_blocklist_listed_by"
msgstr "Your IP or domain <code>{item}</code> is blocklisted on {blocklist_name}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:282
msgid "diagnosis_mail_queue_unavailable"
msgstr "Can not consult number of pending emails in queue"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:283
msgid "diagnosis_mail_queue_unavailable_details"
msgstr "Error: {error}"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py:291
msgid "diagnosis_mail_queue_too_big"
msgstr "Too many pending emails in mail queue ({nb_pending} emails)"

#: src/diagnosers/24-mail.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_mail"
msgstr "Email"

#: src/diagnosers/30-services.py:45
msgid "diagnosis_services_bad_status"
msgstr "Service {service} is {status} :("

#: src/diagnosers/30-services.py:46
msgid "diagnosis_services_bad_status_tip"
msgstr ""
"You can try to <a href='#/services/{service}'>restart the service</a>, "
"and if it doesn't work, have a look at <a href='#/services/{service}'>the"
" service logs in the webadmin</a> (from the command line, you can do this"
" with <cmd>yunohost service restart {service}</cmd> and <cmd>yunohost "
"service log {service}</cmd>)."

#: src/diagnosers/30-services.py:50
msgid "diagnosis_services_conf_broken"
msgstr "Configuration is broken for service {service}!"

#: src/diagnosers/30-services.py:55
msgid "diagnosis_services_running"
msgstr "Service {service} is running!"

#: src/diagnosers/30-services.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_services"
msgstr "Services status check"

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:41
msgid "diagnosis_regenconf_allgood"
msgstr "All configuration files are in line with the recommended configuration!"

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:52
msgid "diagnosis_regenconf_manually_modified"
msgstr ""
"Configuration file <code>{file}</code> appears to have been manually "
"modified."

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:53
msgid "diagnosis_regenconf_manually_modified_details"
msgstr ""
"This is probably OK if you know what you're doing! YunoHost will stop "
"updating this file automatically… But beware that YunoHost upgrades could"
" contain important recommended changes. If you want to, you can inspect "
"the differences with <cmd>yunohost tools regen-conf {category} --dry-run "
"--with-diff</cmd> and force the reset to the recommended configuration "
"with <cmd>yunohost tools regen-conf {category} --force</cmd>"

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:66
msgid "diagnosis_sshd_config_insecure"
msgstr ""
"The SSH configuration appears to have been manually modified, and is "
"insecure because it contains no 'AllowGroups' or 'AllowUsers' directive "
"to limit access to authorized users."

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:78
msgid "diagnosis_sshd_config_inconsistent"
msgstr ""
"It looks like the SSH port was manually modified in /etc/ssh/sshd_config."
" Since YunoHost 4.2, a new global setting 'security.ssh.ssh_port' is "
"available to avoid manually editing the configuration."

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py:79
msgid "diagnosis_sshd_config_inconsistent_details"
msgstr ""
"Please run <cmd>yunohost settings set security.ssh.ssh_port -v "
"YOUR_SSH_PORT</cmd> to define the SSH port, and check <cmd>yunohost tools"
" regen-conf ssh --dry-run --with-diff</cmd> and <cmd>yunohost tools "
"regen-conf ssh --force</cmd> to reset your conf to the YunoHost "
"recommendation."

#: src/diagnosers/70-regenconf.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_regenconf"
msgstr "System configurations"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:56
msgid "diagnosis_ram_verylow"
msgstr ""
"The system has only {available} ({available_percent}%) RAM available! "
"(out of {total})"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:59
msgid "diagnosis_ram_low"
msgstr ""
"The system has {available} ({available_percent}%) RAM available (out of "
"{total}). Be careful."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:62
msgid "diagnosis_ram_ok"
msgstr ""
"The system still has {available} ({available_percent}%) RAM available out"
" of {total}."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:76
msgid "diagnosis_swap_none"
msgstr ""
"The system has no swap at all. You should consider adding at least "
"{recommended} of swap to avoid situations where the system runs out of "
"memory."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:79
msgid "diagnosis_swap_notsomuch"
msgstr ""
"The system has only {total} swap. You should consider having at least "
"{recommended} to avoid situations where the system runs out of memory."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:82
msgid "diagnosis_swap_ok"
msgstr "The system has {total} of swap!"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:83
msgid "diagnosis_swap_tip"
msgstr ""
"Please be careful and aware that if the server is hosting swap on an SD "
"card or SSD storage, it may drastically reduce the life expectancy of the"
" device."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:128
msgid "diagnosis_diskusage_verylow"
msgstr ""
"Storage <code>{mountpoint}</code> (on device <code>{device}</code>) has "
"only {free} ({free_percent}%) space remaining (out of {total}). You "
"should really consider cleaning up some space!"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:133
msgid "diagnosis_diskusage_low"
msgstr ""
"Storage <code>{mountpoint}</code> (on device <code>{device}</code>) has "
"only {free} ({free_percent}%) space remaining (out of {total}). Be "
"careful."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:136
msgid "diagnosis_diskusage_ok"
msgstr ""
"Storage <code>{mountpoint}</code> (on device <code>{device}</code>) still"
" has {free} ({free_percent}%) space left (out of {total})!"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:158
msgid "diagnosis_rootfstotalspace_critical"
msgstr ""
"The root filesystem only has a total of {space} which is quite worrisome!"
" You will likely run out of disk space very quickly! It's recommended to "
"have at least 16 GB for the root filesystem."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:165
msgid "diagnosis_rootfstotalspace_warning"
msgstr ""
"The root filesystem only has a total of {space}. This may be okay, but be"
" careful because ultimately you may run out of disk space quickly… It's "
"recommended to have at least 16 GB for the root filesystem."

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py:181
msgid "diagnosis_processes_killed_by_oom_reaper"
msgstr ""
"Some processes were recently killed by the system because it ran out of "
"memory. This is typically symptomatic of a lack of memory on the system "
"or of a process consuming too much memory. Summary of the processes "
"killed:\n"
"{kills_summary}"

#: src/diagnosers/50-systemresources.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_systemresources"
msgstr "System resources"

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:49
msgid "diagnosis_apps_allgood"
msgstr "All installed apps respect basic packaging practices"

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:69
msgid "diagnosis_apps_issue"
msgstr "An issue was found for app {app}"

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:130
msgid "diagnosis_apps_not_in_app_catalog"
msgstr ""
"This application is not in YunoHost's application catalog. If it was in "
"the past and was removed, you should consider uninstalling this app as it"
" won't receive upgrades and may compromise the integrity and security of "
"your system."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:135
msgid "diagnosis_apps_broken"
msgstr ""
"This application is currently flagged as broken on YunoHost's application"
" catalog. This may be a temporary issue while the maintainers attempt to "
"fix the issue. In the meantime, upgrading this app is disabled."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:137
msgid "diagnosis_apps_bad_quality"
msgstr ""
"This application is currently flagged as broken on YunoHost's application"
" catalog. This may be a temporary issue while the maintainers attempt to "
"fix the issue. In the meantime, upgrading this app is disabled."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:142
msgid "diagnosis_apps_outdated_packaging_format"
msgstr ""
"This app uses a deprecated packaging format and will soon be unsupported "
"by YunoHost. You should really consider upgrading it."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:152
msgid "diagnosis_apps_outdated_ynh_requirement"
msgstr ""
"This app's installed version only requires yunohost >= 2.x, 3.x or 4.x, "
"which tends to indicate that it's not up to date with recommended "
"packaging practices and helpers. You should really consider upgrading it."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:169 src/diagnosers/80-apps.py:176
msgid "diagnosis_apps_deprecated_practices"
msgstr ""
"This app's installed version still uses some very old, deprecated "
"packaging practices. You should really consider upgrading it."

#: src/diagnosers/80-apps.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_apps"
msgstr "Applications"

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:90
msgid "diagnosis_dns_specialusedomain"
msgstr ""
"Domain {domain} is based on a special-use top-level domain (TLD) such as "
".local or .test and is therefore not expected to have actual DNS records."

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:133
msgid "diagnosis_dns_missing_record"
msgstr ""
"According to the recommended DNS configuration, you should add a DNS "
"record with the following info.<br>Type: <code>{type}</code><br>Name: "
"<code>{name}</code><br>Value: <code>{content}</code>"

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:136
msgid "diagnosis_dns_discrepancy"
msgstr ""
"The following DNS record does not seem to follow the recommended "
"configuration:<br>Type: <code>{type}</code><br>Name: "
"<code>{name}</code><br>Current value: <code>{current}</code><br>Expected "
"value: <code>{content}</code>"

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:156
msgid "diagnosis_dns_bad_conf"
msgstr ""
"Some DNS records are missing or incorrect for domain {domain} (category "
"{category})"

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:159
msgid "diagnosis_dns_good_conf"
msgstr ""
"DNS records are correctly configured for domain {domain} (category "
"{category})"

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:177
msgid "diagnosis_dns_try_dyndns_update_force"
msgstr ""
"This domain's DNS configuration should automatically be managed by "
"YunoHost. If that's not the case, you can try to force an update using "
"<cmd>yunohost dyndns update --force</cmd>."

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:180
msgid "diagnosis_dns_point_to_doc"
msgstr ""
"Please check the documentation at <a "
"href='https://doc.yunohost.org/dns_config'>https://doc.yunohost.org/dns_config</a>"
" if you need help configuring DNS records."

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py:292
msgid "diagnosis_domain_expires_in"
msgstr "{domain} expires in {days} days."

#: src/diagnosers/12-dnsrecords.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_dnsrecords"
msgstr "DNS records"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:62
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_hardware"
msgstr "Server hardware architecture is {virt} {arch}"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:69 src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:78
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_hardware_model"
msgstr "Server model is {model}"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:88
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_kernel"
msgstr "Server is running Linux kernel {kernel_version}"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:96
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_host"
msgstr "Server is running Debian {debian_version}"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:112
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_ynh_single_version"
msgstr "{package} version: {version} ({repo})"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:130
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_ynh_main_version"
msgstr "Server is running YunoHost {main_version} ({repo})"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:132
msgid "diagnosis_basesystem_ynh_inconsistent_versions"
msgstr ""
"You are running inconsistent versions of the YunoHost packages… most "
"probably because of a failed or partial upgrade."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:141
msgid "diagnosis_security_vulnerable_to_meltdown"
msgstr "You appear vulnerable to the Meltdown critical security vulnerability"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:142
msgid "diagnosis_security_vulnerable_to_meltdown_details"
msgstr ""
"To fix this, you should upgrade your system and reboot to load the new "
"linux kernel (or contact your server provider if this doesn't work). See "
"https://meltdownattack.com/ for more info."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:154
msgid "diagnosis_package_installed_from_sury"
msgstr "Some system packages should be downgraded"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:155
msgid "diagnosis_package_installed_from_sury_details"
msgstr ""
"Some packages were inadvertendly installed from a third-party repository "
"called Sury. The YunoHost team improved the strategy that handle these "
"packages, but it's expected that some setups that installed PHP7.3 apps "
"while still on Stretch have some remaining inconsistencies. To fix this "
"situation, you should try running the following command: "
"<cmd>{cmd_to_fix}</cmd>"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:162
msgid "diagnosis_backports_in_sources_list"
msgstr ""
"It looks like apt (the package manager) is configured to use the "
"backports repository. Unless you really know what you are doing, we "
"strongly discourage installing packages from backports, because it's "
"likely to create unstabilities or conflicts on your system."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:189
msgid "diagnosis_using_yunohost_testing"
msgstr ""
"<cmd>apt</cmd> (the system's package manager) is currently configured to "
"install any 'testing' upgrade for YunoHost core."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:190
msgid "diagnosis_using_yunohost_testing_details"
msgstr ""
"This is probably OK if you know what you are doing, but pay attention to "
"the release notes before installing YunoHost upgrades! If you want to "
"disable 'testing' upgrades, you should remove the <cmd>testing</cmd> "
"keyword from <cmd>/etc/apt/sources.list.d/yunohost.list</cmd>."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:206
msgid "diagnosis_using_stable_codename"
msgstr ""
"<cmd>apt</cmd> (the system's package manager) is currently configured to "
"install packages from codename 'stable', instead of the codename of the "
"current Debian version (bookworm)."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:207
msgid "diagnosis_using_stable_codename_details"
msgstr ""
"This is usually caused by incorrect configuration from your hosting "
"provider. This is dangerous, because as soon as the next Debian version "
"becomes the new 'stable', <cmd>apt</cmd> will want to upgrade all system "
"packages without going through a proper migration procedure. It is "
"recommended to fix this by editing the apt source for base Debian "
"repository, and replace the <cmd>stable</cmd> keyword by "
"<cmd>bookworm</cmd>. The corresponding configuration file should be "
"<cmd>/etc/apt/sources.list</cmd>, or a file in "
"<cmd>/etc/apt/sources.list.d/</cmd>."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:214
msgid "diagnosis_high_number_auth_failures"
msgstr ""
"There's been a suspiciously high number of authentication failures "
"recently. You may want to make sure that fail2ban is running and is "
"correctly configured, or use a custom port for SSH as explained in "
"https://doc.yunohost.org/security."

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:222
msgid "diagnosis_rfkill_wifi"
msgstr ""
"The Wi-Fi card is disabled and a system warning might prevent app "
"installations"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py:223
msgid "diagnosis_rfkill_wifi_details"
msgstr ""
"This warning sneaks in many command outputs, breaking some apps. It is "
"usually required to specify your country code with the command <code>sudo"
" raspi-config</code>. Here is the error:<br>{rfkill_wifi_error}"

#: src/diagnosers/00-basesystem.py
msgid "diagnosis_description_basesystem"
msgstr "Base system"

